        {
          "name": "1232891-lns-gathering-storm-the-expanse-1cde577d-b494-488a-ad58-50bf321302d8.pdf",
          "bytes": 167260,
          "sha256": "357fe143d739a767c7398fd1c943190d57410dd17d32ef0d5400d67e55e3f4de",
          "text": "3D\n\nM\n\nO\n\nD\n\nEL\n\nO\n\nN\n\nLY\n\nL.N.S. Gathering\nStorm - The\nExpanse\nd\n\ndredeth\n\nVIEW IN BROWSER\nupdated 17. 3. 2025 | published 17. 3. 2025\n\nSummary\nMy design of Laconian Fast Destroyer, as described in the last 3 books of\n\"The Expanse\"\nTabletop Miniatures > Vehicles & Machines\nTags: expanse\nlaconia\n\nmcrn\n\ngatheringstorm\n\nvalkyrie\n\nholden\n\nprotomolecule\n\nduarte\n\nThis is a personal fan art project inspired by the universe of The Expanse.\nAs a professional architect with a passion for science fiction, I wanted to\nreimagine the spaces and structures that might exist in this incredible\nworld. I\u2019ve focused on architectural detail, proportion, and immersive\ndesign described in James S. A. Corey's books.\nAs its Wiki page states: \"The Gathering Storm, or simply the Storm, is a\nLaconian Pulsar-class fast-attack destroyer.\"\nThis is a non-commercial project, made purely out of admiration for the\nseries.\nMore details and info on my ArtStation portfolio: https://\nwww.artstation.com/vrac and YouTube channel: https://www.youtube.com/\n@dredeth\n\n\fModel files\ngathering-storm-3d-print-whole.stl\n\ngathering-storm-3d-print-01-bow.stl\n\ngathering-storm-3d-print-02-middle.stl\n\ngathering-storm-3d-print-03-stern.stl\n\ngathering-storm-3d-print-04-railgun-and-drive-cone.stl\n\nLicense \uf1f9\nThis work is licensed under a\nCreative Commons (4.0 International License)\nAttribution-NonCommercial\n\n\u2716 | Sharing without ATTRIBUTION\n\u2714 | Remix Culture allowed\n\u2716 | Commercial Use\n\u2716 | Free Cultural Works\n\u2716 | Meets Open Definition\n\n\f\f"
        }
      ]
